Install Node.js if it isn't already installed. Open a terminal inside the Day-1-What-is-API folder and run:
npm init -y


Create hello-api.js with this code:

const http = require("http");

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.writeHead(200, {
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
    });

    const data = {
        message: "My first API is working!",
        day: 1,
        topic: "Introduction to API"
    };

    res.end(JSON.stringify(data));
});

server.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log("API running at http://localhost:3000");
});



Run it:
node hello-api.js


Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser. You should see a JSON response similar to:
{
  "message": "My first API is working!",
  "day": 1,
  "topic": "Introduction to API"
}


What did you build? A basic HTTP server that responds with JSON. This is your first API practice; it is not yet a complete REST API.
